TEXT 176 0 Left 3 ;#209 Trifilar transformer, phasing dots on the scope
TEXT 176 64 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LuZh1QnegC4
TEXT 176 112 Left 2 ;Three identical windings on one core. CH2 is probed at its dotted end and CH3 at its
TEXT 176 144 Left 2 ;undotted end, so CH2 follows the primary and CH3 comes out inverted.
TEXT 176 592 Left 2 ;This is the bench setup from Alan's notes page. The dot on each winding marks the terminal
TEXT 176 624 Left 2 ;LTspice treats as corresponding, and all three are drawn the same way up, which is exactly what
TEXT 176 656 Left 2 ;trifilar winding buys you: every wire end on the same side of the core is in phase, so you pick
TEXT 176 688 Left 2 ;a side and dot it.
TEXT 176 736 Left 2 ;L2 is grounded at its undotted end and probed at its dotted end, so CH2 is in phase with CH1.
TEXT 176 768 Left 2 ;L3 is grounded at its dotted end and probed at its undotted end, so CH3 is the mirror image.
TEXT 176 816 Left 2 ;Each winding carries Rser=0.1, which LTspice does not draw. The 47 uH windings, the coupling of
TEXT 176 848 Left 2 ;0.995, the 1 MHz 1 V drive and Rgen are choices: Alan's page gives none of these numbers, and
TEXT 176 880 Left 2 ;Rgen stands for the generator's own 50 ohm output resistance, which his drawing leaves out.
TEXT 1000 160 Left 2 !K1 L1 L2 L3 0.995
TEXT 1000 200 Left 2 !.tran 0 5u 0 1n
TEXT 1000 240 Left 2 !.options plotwinsize=0
TEXT 1000 296 Left 2 !.meas tran vch1 FIND V(ch1) AT 2.25u
TEXT 1000 336 Left 2 !.meas tran vch2 FIND V(ch2) AT 2.25u
TEXT 1000 376 Left 2 !.meas tran vch3 FIND V(ch3) AT 2.25u
TEXT 1000 432 Left 2 !.meas tran ch1_pp PP V(ch1) FROM 2u TO 3u
TEXT 1000 472 Left 2 !.meas tran ch2_pp PP V(ch2) FROM 2u TO 3u
TEXT 1000 512 Left 2 !.meas tran ch3_pp PP V(ch3) FROM 2u TO 3u
